<title>FRANCE: Accor confirms Compass stake sale.</title>
<headline>Accor confirms Compass stake sale.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>French hotel and leisure group Accor confirmed it had sold a 1.89 percent stake in Compass Group Plc on the London stock market, adding it was pleased with the transaction.</p>
<p>&quot;The shareholders' pact allows us to play yo-yo from time to time, we bought twice in the past year and today we sold. The market has been sympathetic recently and the pound has also gained,&quot; a spokeswoman for Accor said.</p>
<p>She declined to give the price of the transaction or any other financial details and had no comment to market talk Accor made a capital gain of 125 million francs on the deal.</p>
</text>
